# Walkthrough: Enhancing Canvas Data Access for AI

In this follow-up section, I have implemented full support for the AI to fetch and analyse core Canvas structural materials including the course syllabus, week-by-week modules, and individual wiki pages.

## Changes Made

### 1. New SQLModels
- **[CanvasPage](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/models/canvas_page.py#9-30)**: Stores the raw HTML and extracted plaintext for Wiki pages on Canvas.
- **[CanvasModule](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/models/canvas_module.py#9-29) & [CanvasModuleItem](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/models/canvas_module.py#31-53)**: Stores the chronological outline of the course and references to files, pages, and assignments within those weeks.
- Added `syllabus_body` directly to the [Course](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/models/course.py#38-66) model.

### 2. Canvas Sync Updates
- Refactored [canvas_sync.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/canvas_sync.py) to now fetch `syllabus_body` during the `/api/v1/courses` call.
- Added two new complex background parsers: [sync_modules](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/canvas_sync.py#507-596) and [sync_pages](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/canvas_sync.py#598-678), which are called in the global [sync_all](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/canvas_sync.py#680-781) block.
- Any fetched [CanvasPage](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/models/canvas_page.py#9-30) is now also natively embedded into the `rag_service` for general [search_module_materials](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/ai_tools.py#308-378) keyword lookups by the AI.

### 3. New AI Executive Tools
I have provided three new specific tools to the LLM agent via [ai_tools.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/ai_tools.py) and [context_assembler.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/context_assembler.py):
- [get_course_syllabus](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/ai_tools.py#978-1007): Instructed as the go-to resource for logistics, grading criteria, and overview questions.
- [get_course_modules_outline](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/ai_tools.py#1009-1052): Instructed to be used to answer questions about the course timeline (e.g. "What are we doing in Week 3?").
- [get_canvas_page_content](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/ai_tools.py#1054-1091): Enables the AI to read specific wiki pages.

## Validation Results
- Python compiler and database initialization routines executed flawlessly.
- `pytest` for AI documents passed all 26 tests, protecting regression. The AI will now begin dynamically fetching and referencing dense course documents!
